GitHub Actions Triggers — A Simple Breakdown

Everything in GitHub Actions starts with a trigger.
No trigger = no automation. Simple as that.

 Flow: Event → Trigger → Workflow → Jobs → Steps

⚡ Common Triggers

1️⃣ Manual (workflow_dispatch)
→ Click "Run workflow" in Actions tab
→ Best for testing & learning

2️⃣ Push (on: push)
→ Triggers when code is pushed
→ Filter to specific branches (e.g. main)
→ Most common in CI/CD

3️⃣ Pull Request (on: pull_request)
→ Runs when a PR is opened or updated
→ Validates code before merging

4️⃣ Schedule (on: schedule)
→ Cron-based — e.g. every Friday 9PM UTC
→ Perfect for planned deploys & maintenance

💡 Simple rule:
Event happens → Trigger fires → Automation runs
